From: WinPad
Subject: [PATCH] wow64win: An atom or a resource id stays as it is.

A 32-bit program names a window class, a menu or a dialog by an atom or a
resource id (MAKEINTATOM, MAKEINTRESOURCE): a value below 64 KB where a
string pointer would be, told apart by IS_INTRESOURCE(). Madeira's
guest_ptr32() adds the guest window base B to every value, so the dialog
class atom 0x8002 of Morrowind Launcher.exe reached NtUserCreateWindowEx
as the UNICODE_STRING Buffer 0x7000008002. IS_INTRESOURCE() was false,
wine_dbgstr_wn read the uncommitted bottom of the guest window, and the
0xc0000005 could not be dispatched ("Exception frame is not in stack
limits"): every dialog-based 32-bit launcher died before its window.

get_str_or_atom() already did this for three arguments; guest_ptr32() and
host_ptr32() now do it for every value, the Buffer of each UNICODE_STRING,
CREATESTRUCT.lpszClass and WNDCLASS menu names included. No guest address
is below 64 KB (Windows keeps that range free, and so does the guest
window). With B == 0 nothing changes.

Applies to willfaust/wine at 257f271 (Madeira 48f9764's wine submodule).
Test: tests/wine-i386/atomclass.c.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wow64win/wow64win_private.h b/dlls/wow64win/wow64win_private.h
index 6bf1074..ca222e0 100644
--- a/dlls/wow64win/wow64win_private.h
+++ b/dlls/wow64win/wow64win_private.h
@@ -74,16 +74,26 @@ static inline ULONG_PTR wow64win_guest_base(void)
     return cached;
 }
 
-/* guest 32-bit address -> host pointer.  NULL stays NULL. */
+/* guest 32-bit address -> host pointer.  NULL stays NULL.
+ *
+ * WinPad: a value below 64 KB stays as it is too. It is no address in a
+ * Windows process (IS_INTRESOURCE is built on that) but an atom or a resource
+ * id: the class of CreateWindowEx (UNICODE_STRING Buffer = MAKEINTATOM),
+ * a menu name in WNDCLASS, lpszClass in CREATESTRUCT. With + B the class atom
+ * 0x8002 of a 32-bit game became 0x7000008002, IS_INTRESOURCE() was false and
+ * NtUserCreateWindowEx read the uncommitted bottom of the guest window
+ * (wine_dbgstr_wn+0x4c, 0xc0000005 that SEH could not dispatch). */
 static inline void *guest_ptr32( ULONG addr )
 {
-    return addr ? (void *)(wow64win_guest_base() + addr) : NULL;
+    if (!(addr >> 16)) return (void *)(ULONG_PTR)addr;
+    return (void *)(wow64win_guest_base() + addr);
 }
 
 /* host pointer -> guest 32-bit address.  NULL stays 0. */
 static inline ULONG host_ptr32( const void *addr )
 {
-    return addr ? (ULONG)((ULONG_PTR)addr - wow64win_guest_base()) : 0;
+    if (!((ULONG_PTR)addr >> 16)) return (ULONG)(ULONG_PTR)addr;  /* atom, id */
+    return (ULONG)((ULONG_PTR)addr - wow64win_guest_base());
 }
 
 static inline ULONG get_ulong( UINT **args ) { return *(*args)++; }
